      "message": "fix(post): a trailing Go home entry merges with the end-of-program home\n\nA Go home last in the program (an entry, or the last op's own after-\naction - both fold into its PARAM AfterOperation home) was written,\nthen the post's close wrote the same reference return again before M30.\nEach built-in post that homes at program end now records where its trip\nhome ended (homedAt = linesWritten(), a new PRELUDE helper) and onClose\nskips its own home when nothing was written after it. Fanuc, Haas,\nMazak, Siemens 840D and Fanuc Lathe; Heidenhain and Tormach refuse a\ntrip home by name, unchanged. Mid-program homes, Suppress and \"Skip\npauses and homes\" are untouched. Decision in\ndocs/decisions/504-trailing-home.md.\n\nFixes #504\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
